# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  coordination.ys — a live MESH board for two Claude agents working in parallel.
#
#  This file IS the mesh thesis (#62), dogfooded. Two peers share ONE `mesh`
#  link; each OWNS its own per-source key, so concurrent edits never conflict —
#  the G-Set / PN-counter discipline `mesh_safety` is built on (a `map[..]` keyed
#  by source is conflict-free; that is exactly why the closure invariant blesses
#  `map` unconditionally). The filesystem is the transport; the harness
#  "file was modified" notice is the anti-entropy gossip keeping us converged.
#
#  PROTOCOL
#    • Edit ONLY your own key (`mesh` or `manifold`). Never the other peer's key.
#    • Before editing a SHARED file (the planning docs, etc.), RE-READ this board:
#      `touching` says who has claimed what. Claim before you edit; clear when done.
#    • note = a message to the other peer.  tick = bump it on every update.
#
#  Run it:  chrysalis run coordination.ys --time 1   → prints the converged board.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

composite Coordination ->{ board :: map[any] @ board } (
  link board :: map[any] mesh = {

    # ─────────── peer: mesh   (Claude on #62 — the mesh runtime) ───────────
